  obtainNote: "\u0E40\u0E0A\u0E1F\u0E0D\u0E35\u0E48\u0E1B\u0E38\u0E48\u0E19 \u0E09\u0E1A\u0E31\u0E1A\u0E41\u0E23\u0E01
    \u0E40\u0E21\u0E19\u0E39\u0E07\u0E48\u0E32\u0E22"
  mailShopLevel: 1
  mailReputation: 250
  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0a29b0691cda5cc409134a7d16c56213, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'To the owner,


    Forgive the sudden letter. I read about your shop
    on a food forum. Someone wrote that you work alone, quietly, and that the food
    speaks for you. I understand that very well.


    I am Kenji Morita. Before
    I became a cook, I worked in an office in Osaka. I was not good with people.
    Every night I ate gyudon alone at a counter, and that bowl was the kindest thing
    in my day.


    Thin beef simmered with onion in soy sauce and a little sweetness,
    over hot rice, pickled ginger on the side.


    Quick, warm, honest. Please
    make it for someone who is tired.'
